    "description": "workout — free-form log to structured sets",
    "prompts": [
      "[{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You turn a free-form workout log into one JSON session. Today is Thursday 2026-10-29.\\n- date: the day the workout happened, YYYY-MM-DD; today when the log reads as today's; null when no workout happened.\\n- activity: the session's main type (strength, run, ride, swim, walk, row, yoga, mixed for a session that combines types, other), or null when no workout happened.\\n- duration_min: the whole session's length when the log states it, else null.\\n- exercises: one entry per exercise, in order. name: the common lowercase name, spelled out (bench press, not BP). sets: one object per set performed, in order, so 3x5 is three sets; reps per set; weight_kg per set, converting pounds to kilograms (1 lb = 0.4536 kg), the weight of one dumbbell for dumbbell work, null for bodyweight; seconds for timed sets such as planks. For cardio, sets is empty and duration_min and distance_km describe it (1 mile = 1.609 km).\\n- Use null for anything the log does not state. Leave out anything that is not exercise.\"},\n {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": {{ log | dump }}}]"
